   "seed": "# commerce_analytics world seed: a shop's nightly CDC extracts -> raw -> dbt\n# star schema + semantic layer -> Power BI / Tableau / Sigma dashboards.\ntheme: commerce_analytics    # world/world/themes/<name>/\nseed: 11\nvtime_start: \"2025-01-01T00:00:00Z\"\n# 425 nightly extracts: dt=2024-12-31 (the cutover snapshot: accounts and\n# catalogue, no orders) then dt=2025-01-01 .. dt=2026-02-28. Fourteen months of\n# orders, so last-year measures exist for January and February 2026. The world\n# clock opens at 2026-03-02T00:00Z, a Monday - business day 1 of the February\n# close.\ndays: 425\n\n# Scale. Every key is optional (gen.DEFAULTS); these are the defaults, spelled\n# out. Build time is dominated by dbt, not by volume - a 2x seed builds in about\n# the same time.\ncustomers: 220               # accounts on the platform at cutover\nsignup_pct: 18               # chance per day of a new account (a second at a quarter of it)\nupdate_pct: 9                # chance per day that one account is upgraded a segment\norders_per_day: [20, 60]     # base range, scaled by weekday, month, peak days and growth\nlines_per_order: [1, 4]\ncancel_pct: 6                # 70% the same day, the rest the next day\nrefund_pct: 4                # 3 to 45 days after the order\ngrowth_pct: 20               # year-over-year order volume growth\n\ngit_author: \"Analytics Engineering <analytics@example.com>\"\nnative: true\nfiles: {formats: [parquet]}\nprofile:\n  name: da/laptop\n  slots: [files, notebook, warehouse, transform, bi, human]\n  plugs: {bi: [powerbi, sigma, tableau]}\n",
